<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈdʒuːmuːɑː">Jumu'ah</phoneme> briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">13032026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Iranian drones struck Dubai's financial district on Friday, the twenty-first consecutive day of the war between Iran and the United States.</s> <s>Tehran's targeting has moved methodically inward — from the city's airport and port, to the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="pɑːm dʒuːˈmeɪrə">Palm Jumeirah</phoneme> resort island, and now to the towers where global finance operates.</s> <s>Dubai's three and a half million residents, most of them migrant workers from South and Southeast Asia, have no embassy evacuation and nowhere to go.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Israel bombed a refugee camp in central Beirut, killing twelve people — the latest strike in a campaign that has killed nearly seven hundred since the ceasefire collapsed.</s> <s>Defense Minister Israel Katz then threatened to annex Lebanese territory and ordered the military to prepare for a ground expansion.</s> <s>More than seven hundred thousand people are displaced across Lebanon, and evacuation orders now cover a tenth of the country.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's air force struck homes in Kabul overnight, killing four — the first time Islamabad has directly bombed the Afghan capital.</s> <s>Pakistan declared war on Afghanistan two weeks ago, accusing the Taliban of sheltering <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tɛˈriːk iː tɑːlɪˈbɑːn">Tehrik-i-Taliban</phoneme> fighters responsible for attacks inside Pakistan itself.</s> <s>Strikes have expanded to Kandahar and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="pækˈtiːə">Paktia</phoneme>, displacing sixty-six thousand Afghans, as China attempts mediation.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Sudan's paramilitary Rapid Support Forces bombed civilian homes in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌkɔːrdəˈfɑːn">Kordofan</phoneme>, using drones to drive displacement from the country's agricultural and mineral heartland.</s> <s>A potential fracture opened within the RSF itself: <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌrɪˈzeɪɡɑːt">Rizeigat</phoneme> tribal leader <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmuːsə məˈdiːboʊ">Musa Madibo</phoneme> broke from the RSF's commander this week — a defection that could reshape the war's balance.</s> <s>The world's worst humanitarian crisis continues while global attention is fixed on the Gulf.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A report by the Armed Conflict Location and Event Data Project found that United States forces struck foreign countries six hundred and sixty-three times in 2025 — a fifty percent rise over the previous year and the highest total since 2011.</s> <s>More than one thousand people died in operations that lacked any congressional authorization.</s> <s>All of this occurred under President Trump, who ran on ending foreign wars.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>American intelligence agencies assessed Iran's government as stable and in firm control — a finding that directly contradicts Washington's stated aim of forcing Tehran to capitulate through bombardment.</s> <s>Multiple assessments offer what officials describe as consistent analysis pointing the same direction.</s> <s>The Trump administration has not stated what it will do if the strategy fails to produce collapse.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Iran has reduced Hormuz shipping from one hundred and thirty-eight daily transits to five — and this week granted Indian-flagged tankers passage that other nations were denied, revealing the blockade as a political tool with a guest list.</s> <s>A coordinated release of four hundred million barrels from international strategic reserves failed to push oil below one hundred dollars a barrel.</s> <s>Every dollar above eighty transfers wealth from oil-importing nations in the Global South to producers, with no end in sight.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Three major financial firms evacuated their Dubai staff this week.</s> <s>The Philippines urged Southeast Asian nations to position the region as an investment safe haven for capital fleeing the war, but whether the region can absorb that capital depends on whether it can first manage its own surging oil import costs — a dependency that cuts directly against the pitch.</s> <s>For the Association of Southeast Asian Nations, the war is both an opportunity and a bill arriving at the same time.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The United States opened trade investigations against dozens of nations under a 1974 law that grants the president unilateral tariff authority, bypassing courts and Congress.</s> <s>Beijing called the probes political manipulation.</s> <s>A United States-China treasury meeting is scheduled for the fifteenth of March in France — a test of whether economic diplomacy can survive the same administration that launched the investigations.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The World Bank is investing one hundred and thirty-seven million dollars to connect five point two million West Africans to broadband across three of the world's least-connected nations, where power grids are too unreliable to sustain consistent internet access.</s> <s>The investment arrives as artificial intelligence is already eliminating entry-level digital jobs in better-connected economies.</s> <s>Whether connectivity alone can build economic resilience is a question these nations will have to answer for themselves.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China's fifteenth five-year plan sets a seventeen percent cut in carbon intensity — not absolute emissions — meaning total output can still rise as the economy expands.</s> <s>Beijing has not set a coal phase-out date and continues to permit the expansion of coal-chemical industries.</s> <s>Under this framework, China's emissions could grow by six percent even as its intensity falls.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Britain closed its last coal power plant in September 2024, sending total emissions to their lowest level since eighteen seventy-two — a four-hundred-year low.</s> <s>Coal accounted for sixty percent of a two point four percent drop in United Kingdom emissions last year.</s> <s>The country is still falling short, achieving only sixty percent of the annual reduction needed to reach net zero by 2050.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Chinese chipmaker <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈkæmbrɪkɒn">Cambricon</phoneme> paid its first dividend after recording two billion yuan in profit — a milestone made possible by American export controls that blocked Nvidia from selling chips to China.</s> <s>Data centers across the country migrated to Cambricon's processors, which now run DeepSeek and other leading Chinese artificial intelligence models.</s> <s>If controls tighten further, Cambricon becomes the country's only option at scale.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Despite Australia's ban on social media for under-sixteens, one in five Australian teenagers still uses TikTok, routing around age-gating through virtual private networks that no government has yet blocked.</s> <s>Unlike alcohol or tobacco, social media runs inside every smartphone and follows users across every border.</s> <s>The European Union, the United Kingdom, and several American states are watching Australia's results before deciding whether to attempt the same.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</speak>